{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":484713,"duration_api_ms":480945,"num_turns":16,"result":"All clean — the only clippy warnings are pre-existing in `tank_harness` (not in scope).\n\n**Results: 38/38 tests pass, fmt clean, clippy clean.**\n\nNow producing the ExecutionPayload JSON for round 4:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"contract\": \"plan_and_implement\",\n  \"project_id\": \"tanksim-6e5.4.3\",\n  \"task_title\": \"Integrate CO2 gas exchange with aeration, surface exchange, and ambient coupling\",\n  \"completion_round\": 4,\n\n  \"plan\": {\n    \"amendment_id\": \"r4-sa-v-normalization\",\n    \"summary\": \"Fix gas-exchange scaling so total O2/CO2 surface flux depends on exposed surface area instead of water volume. Add a reference SA/V constant calibrated to the default tank geometry (1000 cm² / 19 L) and normalise the raw K_LA by the ratio of the actual SA/V to this reference. Update the volume-independence test to assert equal surface flux (total mass) and faster concentration change in the shallower tank.\",\n    \"steps\": [\n      \"Add REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L constant (1000.0/19.0) to dissolved_oxygen.rs\",\n      \"Multiply raw_kla by (sa_v / REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L) in compute_o2_kla so gas flux is area-proportional\",\n      \"Rewrite test_co2_exchange_independent_of_tank_volume to assert equal surface flux and faster concentration change in shallow tank\",\n      \"Run all co2_exchange, chemistry, dissolved_oxygen tests — verify 38/38 pass\",\n      \"Verify cargo fmt and cargo clippy are clean\"\n    ],\n    \"files_touched\": [\n      \"crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs\",\n      \"crates/tank_core/tests/co2_exchange.rs\"\n    ],\n    \"risk_notes\": \"compute_o2_kla is used by both O2 and CO2 paths. For the default geometry (open-top, 40×25 cm, 3 cm substrate → 19 L), the SA/V ratio equals the reference, so the multiplier is 1.0 — all existing tests that use default geometry are unaffected. Non-default geometries now correctly scale gas transfer by surface area.\"\n  },\n\n  \"edits\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs\",\n      \"description\": \"Add REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L constant and SA/V normalization to compute_o2_kla\",\n      \"diff_summary\": \"Added const REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L: f64 = 1000.0 / 19.0 (lines 9-16). In compute_o2_kla, after computing raw_kla, compute sa_v = surface_area_cm2() / volume_l and return raw_kla * (sa_v / REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L) instead of bare raw_kla (lines 52-53).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"crates/tank_core/tests/co2_exchange.rs\",\n      \"description\": \"Rewrite test_co2_exchange_independent_of_tank_volume to assert physically correct invariants\",\n      \"diff_summary\": \"Replaced the old equal-concentration-change assertion with two assertions: (1) surface flux (total DIC mass change) approximately equal between shallow and deep tanks (< 10% relative diff), (2) concentration change faster in the shallower tank (shallow > deep × 1.1).\"\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"verification\": {\n    \"tests_run\": \"cargo test --test co2_exchange --test chemistry --test dissolved_oxygen\",\n    \"tests_passed\": 38,\n    \"tests_failed\": 0,\n    \"test_breakdown\": {\n      \"co2_exchange\": \"12/12 passed\",\n      \"chemistry\": \"21/21 passed\",\n      \"dissolved_oxygen\": \"5/5 passed\"\n    },\n    \"fmt_clean\": true,\n    \"clippy_clean\": true,\n    \"clippy_notes\": \"Only pre-existing warnings in tank_harness (items_after_test_module, len_zero) — not in scope for this task.\"\n  },\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"notes\": \"The SA/V normalization is the architecturally significant change in this round. By calibrating to REFERENCE_SA_V_CM2_PER_L = 1000/19 ≈ 52.63 cm²/L (the default tank with substrate), the multiplier is exactly 1.0 for default-geometry tests, preserving all existing behavior. For non-default geometries, gas transfer now correctly scales: two tanks with the same footprint but different fill heights exchange the same total mass per hour, with the shallower tank seeing faster concentration change. The fix applies to both O2 and CO2 because compute_co2_kla delegates to compute_o2_kla.\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3a6e0fba-419d-4c21-8162-56b82cdcb1dc","total_cost_usd":2.5034709999999993,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":181390,"cache_read_input_tokens":1184462,"output_tokens":22099,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":181390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":1320,"outputTokens":26894,"cacheReadInputTokens":1349867,"cacheCreationInputTokens":183934,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.5034709999999993,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b5aeabda-31fe-4fa3-874e-d0bd6bbcfbfd"}
